From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 22:24:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: guard station count during recovery

Firmware recovery removes the driver's peers and resets num_stations before
mac80211 has finished reconciling its saved station state. A subsequent
station removal can therefore decrement the unsigned counter from zero.

Once the counter underflows, ath12k rejects every station re-added by
mac80211 because the wrapped value is greater than max_num_stations. This
leaves the AP unusable even though firmware restart itself completed.

Do not decrement an already empty station count. This follows the guard
used by Qualcomm's downstream Mode-1 recovery implementation and is also
safe for normal station teardown paths.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -6971,6 +6971,9 @@ static void ath12k_mac_dec_num_stations(
 
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(ath12k_ar_to_hw(ar)->wiphy);
 
+	if (!ar->num_stations)
+		return;
+
 	if (arvif->ahvif->vdev_type == WMI_VDEV_TYPE_STA && !sta->tdls)
 		return;
 
